  re-wrapped the result, so every roll turn crossing the 0/360
  boundary (e.g. 350° to 20°) passed through 370..380° mid-turn and
  the clients, which display van_r as-is, showed it (same defect class
  as the B2 heading fix in 2026.09.24.02). The roll interpolation was
  extracted to nav_roll_at in the same pure, dependency-free module
  (src/server/nav_math.c, include/nav_math.h), which takes the
  shortest-arc delta and re-wraps the result back into [0, 360);
  handle_pos now normalizes the requested roll through nav_wrap_heading
  before storing target_r, and the "already aligned" fast-path check
  wraps the roll delta like it already did for the heading, so the
  short timer also works across the boundary. The wrap is display-only
  — it is the same angle, so the shield basis (calculate_shield_index
  uses roll through sin/cos) and the 3D views are unchanged.
